      "role": "user",
      "content": "I am currently working on a comparative study regarding the morphological density of Uralic languages, specifically looking at the way discrete functional units interact within complex agglutinative strings. I find the \"agency\" of these individual morphemes—how they arrive to modify a stem and trigger phonological shifts—to be quite fascinating from a structural perspective.\n\nCould you assist me with a rigorous segmentation of the following Finnish forms? I am looking for a breakdown of the root and each successive morphemic unit (case, number, possession, etc.), as well as a description of the morphophonemic changes that occur when these small components are layered together.\n\n1. *kaupungeissammekin*\n2. *kirjoittaisitko*\n3. *taloissammeko*\n\nPlease focus on the precise mechanics of how these individual units influence their neighbors at the boundaries.",
